Given p, g and y, the following routine searches the subgroup generated by g. It uses constant auxiliary storage and performs at most p - 1 modular multiplications.

def discrete_log(p, g, y):
    z = 1
    for x in range(p - 1):
        if z == y:
            return x
        z = (z * g) % p
    return None

For p = 23, g = 5 and y = 8, it returns 6. If the order of g is known, replace p - 1 by that order. This algorithm supplies a baseline against which a collision-based method can be compared.
